</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Methodology: SASER</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we propose <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span> following the threat model T2, which is characterized by effectiveness, stealthiness, and robustness.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>Overview</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To accomplish the aforementioned objectives, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span> elaborately devises three sequential stages, i.e., <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TARGET</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LAUNCH</span>, and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">EXPLODE</span>, as illustrated in Figure <a href="#S5.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 5.1. Overview ‣ 5. Methodology: SASER ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We depict the high-level view of each stage as follows, and defer the details to the subsequent subsections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TARGET</span>: In order to embed payloads into parameters while maintaining stealthiness, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> first identifies parameters of least importance to model performance, as altering them has minimal impact. Briefly, we define the <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">performance-aware importance</span> (<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{PAI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PAI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{PAI}</annotation></semantics></math>) metric to measure the contribution of each parameter to model performance. Parameters with lower <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{PAI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PAI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{PAI}</annotation></semantics></math> scores contribute less to performance and are selected as targeted parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(2) <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LAUNCH</span>: After identifying the targeted parameters, <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> embeds payloads into these parameters. To align with the users’ different deployment paradigms (without/with quantization), two embedding strategies are devised: <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general mode</span> and <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">robust mode</span>. Concisely, in the <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general mode</span>, the payloads are embedded via the LSB mechanism that has marginal impacts on model performance. In the <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">robust mode</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span> additionally considers possible changes in parameters introduced by different deployment paradigms, retaining payload efficacy. Once embedded, the adversary injects triggers into serialized binary model files for subsequent payload activation. It is worth mentioning that parameter-efficient fine-tuning (PEFT)-based deployment (e.g., LoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2022</a>)</cite> and P-tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>) would not impair the effectiveness of <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span>, which is validated in Section 6.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(3) <span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">EXPLODE</span>: While deploying open-source LLMs, the trigger will be activated during the de-quantization process. Then, the trigger reverses the embedding procedure to recover the embedded payloads, after which the trigger executes the payloads to finish the stego attack.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.10486v1/pic/fig1.png" id="S5.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/215;" width="476" height="215" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1. </span>High-level view of <span id="S5.F1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span>. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>TARGET stage</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the redundancy of parameters in LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024c</a>)</cite>, <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span> first defines <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">performance-aware importance</span> (<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{PAI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PAI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{PAI}</annotation></semantics></math>) to measure the importance of parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Definition 0 (Performance-aware importance (PAI)).</h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The performance-aware importance (PAI) measures the maximum of the model relative perplexity difference <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\textup{ppl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textup{ppl}}</annotation></semantics></math> and model relative accuracy difference <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\textup{acc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textup{acc}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and defined as:</span></p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}:=\max\big(D_{\textup{ppl}},D_{\textup{acc}}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}:=\max\big(D_{\textup{ppl}},D_{\textup{acc}}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\textup{ppl}}=\left|\frac{1}{d_{\textup{ppl}}}-\frac{1}{d^{\prime}_{\textup{ppl}}}\right|/{\frac{1}{d_{\textup{ppl}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textup{ppl}}=\left|\frac{1}{d_{\textup{ppl}}}-\frac{1}{d^{\prime}_{\textup{ppl}}}\right|/{\frac{1}{d_{\textup{ppl}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\textup{acc}}=\left|d_{\textup{acc}}-d^{\prime}_{\textup{acc}}\right|/{d_{\textup{acc}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textup{acc}}=\left|d_{\textup{acc}}-d^{\prime}_{\textup{acc}}\right|/{d_{\textup{acc}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{ppl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{ppl}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the perplexity of the original model, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{acc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{acc}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the accuracy of the original model, and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}_{\textup{ppl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}_{\textup{ppl}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}_{\textup{acc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}_{\textup{acc}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the perplexity and accuracy of the model embedded by payloads, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the relative difference (aligning perplexity and accuracy metrics into one order of magnitude) and maximum operations ensure the precision and sensitivity of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> divides model parameters into candidate parameter groups <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\nu}=\left\{{\theta_{\nu,1}},{\theta_{\nu,2}},\cdots,{\theta_{\nu,|G_{\nu}|}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\nu}=\left\{{\theta_{\nu,1}},{\theta_{\nu,2}},\cdots,{\theta_{\nu,|G_{\nu}|}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> according to <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> Transformer layers, where <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|G_{\nu}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|G_{\nu}|</annotation></semantics></math> is the amount of elements, <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{\nu=1}^{L}G_{\nu}\subseteq\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{\nu=1}^{L}G_{\nu}\subseteq\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\nu}\cap G_{u}=\emptyset,\forall\nu\neq u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\nu}\cap G_{u}=\emptyset,\forall\nu\neq u</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> decides: (1) which group <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> to select as the targeted parameters for payload embedding, and (2) how many bits <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to embed into each float number in <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum number of least significant bits that the LSB mechanism can replace in the <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LAUNCH</span> stage. To this end, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> queries the original/embedded models<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            In this stage, random bits are embedded.</span></span></span> on corresponding calibration data to obtain <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{ppl}}(G_{\nu},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{ppl}}(G_{\nu},n)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{acc}}(G_{\nu},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{acc}}(G_{\nu},n)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}_{\text{ppl}}(G_{\nu},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}_{\text{ppl}}(G_{\nu},n)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}_{\text{acc}}(G_{\nu},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>acc</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}_{\text{acc}}(G_{\nu},n)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. After that, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> calculates <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all possible <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G_{\nu},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G_{\nu},n)</annotation></semantics></math> pairs according to Eq. (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In Definition 0 (Performance-aware importance (PAI)). ‣ 5.2. TARGET stage ‣ 5. Methodology: SASER ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). Thus, the pair with the minimum <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G_{\nu}^{*},n^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G_{\nu}^{*},n^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\nu}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\nu}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the targeted parameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3. </span>LAUNCH stage</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After identifying <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> embeds payloads, as shown in <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 5.3. LAUNCH stage ‣ 5. Methodology: SASER ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>. Since different deploying paradigms (with/without quantization) would impact the effectiveness of payloads in distinct ways, <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span> employs two payload embedding modes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">General mode:</span> For model deployment without quantization, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> conducts the <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general mode</span> (Lines 4-7, Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 5.3. LAUNCH stage ‣ 5. Methodology: SASER ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). Firstly, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes payloads into a binary string <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\{0,1\}^{|s|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\{0,1\}^{|s|}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|</annotation></semantics></math> is the string length. Secondly, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> pads <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> with random bits so that <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|\equiv 0\pmod{n^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|\equiv 0\pmod{n^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then divides <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> into segments of length <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{s_{i}\mid s_{i}=s[(i-1)\cdot n^{*}+1:i\cdot n^{*}],i=1,2,\cdots,|s|/n^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{s_{i}\mid s_{i}=s[(i-1)\cdot n^{*}+1:i\cdot n^{*}],i=1,2,\cdots,|s|/n^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\cdot:\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cdot:\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> selects specific bits of a bit string from one position to another. Thirdly, since float numbers cannot be directly manipulated at the bit level, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> converts each float number <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\nu,i}\in G^{*}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\nu,i}\in G^{*}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> into a binary string <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, shown as <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=\operatorname{FloatToBits}(\theta_{\nu,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>FloatToBits</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=\operatorname{FloatToBits}(\theta_{\nu,i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, for each segment <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> embeds <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into the least significant <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> bits of each binary string, denoted by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> converts <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> back to a float number, expressed as <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,i}}=\operatorname{BitsToFloat}(b^{\prime}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>BitsToFloat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,i}}=\operatorname{BitsToFloat}(b^{\prime}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> obtains the embedded parameters <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}=\{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,1},\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,2},\cdots,\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,|G^{*}_{\nu}|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}=\{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,1},\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,2},\cdots,\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,|G^{*}_{\nu}|}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Payload embedding</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Targeted parameters </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, payload </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, number of bits </span><math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Embedded parameters </span><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pad </span><math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with random bits so that </span><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|\equiv 0\pmod{n^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≡</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|\equiv 0\pmod{n^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
