            <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg1.l16.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l16.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg1.l17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}=\{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,1},\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,2},\cdots,\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,|G^{*}_{\nu}|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}=\{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,1},\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,2},\cdots,\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,|G^{*}_{\nu}|}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l18.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Robust mode:</span> To mitigate the ill-effect of quantization during the model deployment phase, <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> conducts the following operations to ensure the effectiveness of embedded payloads (Lines 9-13, Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 5.3. LAUNCH stage ‣ 5. Methodology: SASER ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). After segmenting <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> quantizes the float number <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\nu,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\nu,i}</annotation></semantics></math> into an integer, shown as <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{\nu,i}\leftarrow\text{Q}(\theta_{\nu,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Q</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{\nu,i}\leftarrow\text{Q}(\theta_{\nu,i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> sequentially conducts the <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">to-bits</span> conversion, embedding, and back-conversion operations similar to the <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general mode</span>. Finally, <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> de-quantizes the embedded parameter <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}^{\prime}_{\nu,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}^{\prime}_{\nu,i}</annotation></semantics></math> back to a float number, shown as <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,i}}\leftarrow\text{Q}^{-1}\left(\hat{\theta}^{\prime}_{\nu,i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\theta^{\prime}_{\nu,i}}\leftarrow\text{Q}^{-1}\left(\hat{\theta}^{\prime}_{\nu,i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence obtains the embedded parameters <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is worth mentioning that <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TARGET</span> stage is calculated on top of quantized parameters for the <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">robust</span> mode.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">After payload embedding, <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> replaces <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the entire embedded model parameters <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> injects triggers into serialized model parameters <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(\Theta^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\Theta^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> following common trigger injection methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">HiddenLayer, 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. In particular, the number of LSB bits <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and payload length <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|</annotation></semantics></math> are also recorded in the trigger for later payload extraction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4. </span>EXPLODE stage</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the model deployment phase, users download <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S({\Theta}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S({\Theta}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> from public repositories, and deploy the model with/without quantization. Then, the user’s operating system de-serializes <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S({\Theta}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S({\Theta}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Theta}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Theta}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereby the injected trigger is de-serialized and activated. Next, the trigger acquires <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|</annotation></semantics></math> to extract the embedded payloads <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> through <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 5.4. EXPLODE stage ‣ 5. Methodology: SASER ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>. Specifically, the trigger converts every <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\nu,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\nu,i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by calculating <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=\operatorname{FloatToBits}(\theta_{\nu,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>FloatToBits</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=\operatorname{FloatToBits}(\theta_{\nu,i})</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=\operatorname{IntToBits}(\theta_{\nu,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>IntToBits</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=\operatorname{IntToBits}(\theta_{\nu,i})</annotation></semantics></math>, depending on the embedding mode, i.e., <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general</span> or <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">robust</span>. Afterwards, the trigger extracts the payload segment <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from the least <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> bits of <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, shown as <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{i}\leftarrow b_{i}[|b_{i}|-n^{*}+1:|b_{i}|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\leftarrow b_{i}[|b_{i}|-n^{*}+1:|b_{i}|]</annotation></semantics></math>. All segments <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i},i=1,\cdots,|s|/n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i},i=1,\cdots,|s|/n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are concatenated orderly to recover the payload <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, trigger executes <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> to complete the stego attack.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Payload extraction</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Embed parameters </span><math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, number of bits </span><math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, length of payload </span><math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Extracted payloads </span><math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> to </span><math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|/n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|/n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg2.l3.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
