<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix: Results of <span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SASER</span> with <span id="A1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">robust model</span></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We plot the attack performance in the setting of 8-bit quantization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grouping methods of targeted parameters.</span> As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Results of SASER with robust model ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> increases along with the increase of <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> from 0 to 1 across all grouping methods, which is in line with the results in the <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general mode</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.10486v1/grains_8.svg" id="A1.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/160;" width="229" height="160"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span><span id="A1.F7.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">LLaMA2-7B</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.10486v1/grains_8_glm.svg" id="A1.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/160;" width="229" height="160"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><span id="A1.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">ChatGLM3-6B</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7. </span><math id="A1.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> of grouping methods with <math id="A1.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> ranging from 1 to 8. We set <math id="A1.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="MLP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">MLP</annotation></semantics></math> matrices as the target matrices for the name-base and matrix-base, and select random layer for the layer-base. Results are averaged over 3 runs with different random seeds.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LSB numbers.</span> Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Results of SASER with robust model ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> of LLaMA2-7B and ChatGLM3-6B with <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> ranging from 1 to 8. For most layers, <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases sharply when <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, payloads with a size no more than 37.5% of the model size can be embedded without detection.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F8.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.10486v1/pai_llama_q8_mmlu.png" id="A1.F8.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/176;" width="229" height="176" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span><span id="A1.F8.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">LLaMA2-7B</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F8.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.10486v1/pai_glm_q8_mmlu.png" id="A1.F8.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/176;" width="229" height="176" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><span id="A1.F8.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">ChatGLM3-6B</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8. </span><math id="A1.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> of models on MMLU with 8-bit quantization. Results are averaged over 3 runs with different random seeds.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Distribution of vulnerable parameters.</span> Figure <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Results of SASER with robust model ‣ SASER: Stego attacks on open-source LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> illustrates more perturbation and uncertainty of <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{PAI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>PAI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{PAI}}</annotation></semantics></math> compared to the <span id="A1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">general mode</span>. The reason behind this observation is that integer values have more variability than floating-point values under LSB embedding methods with the same random bits, impacting model performance to a larger extent.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
